  "name": "Pokémon Diamond & Pearl Battle Festa 2006",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Pokémon Diamond & Pearl Battle Festa★2006 celebrated the new Diamond & Pearl games and card series, in place of Battle Road's autumn season that year. It visited four venues between 25 November and 17 December 2006: Kobe International Exhibition Hall, Port Messe Nagoya, the West Japan General Exhibition Center and Pacifico Yokohama.\n\nIts main tournament, Battle Road Stadium DP, was played with 30-card decks: players climbed stages of two and then three straight wins to face a researcher of the Pokémon Card Laboratory, the game's developers. Every entrant got Manaphy 003/DP-P, and anyone who beat the researcher won a cosmos holo Championship Arena, with new art by Ryo Ueda of Dialga and Palkia facing each other in the arena. At the Festa's card game information corner, readers could exchange the mount that Riolu came on in the December 2006 CoroCoro Comic for Lucario 002/DP-P.",
